Android port: touch-friendly widgets.

* Context menus scroll (a long menu ran off a phone screen) and close only on a tap outside them.
* Submenus inside such a menu unfold in place on a tap. egui's own submenus open while the pointer
  hovers, and a finger "hovers" whatever it touches, so they opened and activated by accident.
* Sliders: only the thumb takes a touch (a finger-sized grab area). A tap on the track does nothing
  and a drag that starts on the track scrolls the panel, so scrolling past a slider never changes
  it. A drag moves the thumb by the finger's travel, so the value never jumps to the touch point.
  Typing a value (tap the number) is unchanged.
